{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/442627-balefire-stories-your-experiences-with-changeling-the-dreaming","id":442627,"title":"Balefire Stories (Your experiences with Changeling: The Dreaming)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-15T09:19:53-07:00","id":442627,"title":"Balefire Stories (Your experiences with Changeling: The Dreaming)","content":"I don't know, if similar topic existed, but it wasn't interested and fell down, but, in recent news, that work on Changeling 20th Anniversary Edition begins I wanted to start it, so you could share a story about how you learned about CtD (it was back in 95' or later), couple of fun stories about your adventures. How have you survived long winter nights after Time of Judgement? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Probably, there will be some new writers and and creators, working on this project, who started as fans. Dunno. Let's celebrate our acquaintance with Changelings. I'll start in first comment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 03-15-2015, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:20:25-07:00","id":442633,"title":"","content":"When I heard about Changeling, I was playing my very first tabletop rpg, at summer of 2008. I've graduated school, played Sabbat Assamite, talked with folks six or more years older than me, and enjoyed it very much. Such words, as 'Faerie' or 'Glamour' didn't made me flinch at the time. Until 2009-2010, when I created that Malkavian primogen of San-Francisco, who was deluded, that he's Oberon. He was half-shakespearean type, half-fishmalk type, not my best character, but fun, though. Then, I've become acquainted with fan translation of second ed. Changeling core book (thank you, A., wherever you are now)!<br /> <br /> Since then I had only two Changeling games (and two, as ST, so four in summary). That's <i>how easy</i> to find die hard fan of Changeling here. First campaign was set in San-Francisco and were loosely based on Toybox adventure (without any of NPC's stats!). It was a story about pair of sidhe court wizard's apprentices. My character was named Lysander aep Eiluned - orphan of war, who was raised by his teacher, baron Falstaff aep Eiluned (court wizard, himself) in his own wizard's tower, which was hidden inside of pipe of very old steel plant. Second apprentice was glome, named Rowta/Rauta (I don't know, how to spell it), who fled ranks of Glome military to become alien in court of changelings. There was also chimeric butterfly of mindshattering beauty and undying love for puzzles and riddles - Adonis, and I've played it too, for the most part.<br /> <br /> It was quite a stretch to allow my character to have Metamorphosis Art at 5. Let's face it - some Arts was severely underpowered, and some others was <b>over</b>povered like hell and Metamorphosis was <i>latter</i>. And, besides, it was sooo wizard'ey, that I practically begged ST to allow it. This was his first face to face table top game, so he agreed for his sorrow. And this addition changed <b>a lot</b> about the story. We haven't killed <i>any</i> of chimeric creatures from the trunk. Under protection of mighty Rauta, Lysander turned dragon into giant sheep, to put it into taxi's baggage compartment, turned bear into cute hamster-like mini bear, and some unfriendly chinese dragons - into turtles, three meter sized ones. Among other things, Rauta met and inspired urban fantasy author, struggling against writer's block, Lyzander fought really tough battle with agents of banality (two lecturers from [Church of Habologists], if you know, what I mean) at esoteri\u0441 center &quot;Chorus Eye&quot;, where he taught &quot;History of mythology and folklore&quot;. Then, we overdid containment measures for captive red cap - actually, there isn't much you can do to stop cantrip casting, if captive has appropriate Arts and Realms: bunk could be anything, we mused, so... some duct tape was used. Poor <i>Slique</i>...<br /> <br /> And after that was immortal scene of three dozens Shadow Court's changelings attacking count Aeon's freehold. With us in it. <b>&quot;Big mistake.&quot;</b> Storyteller said, he didn't expected from us to side with count, when we learned about heartbraking betrayal of our teacher. He didn't expected from us to save count at all. And also, he didn't expect me to burn 2 dots of <i>permanent</i> Glamour to turn into mythical creature (&quot;Dragon Enters&quot;, you shadow scum!), effectively destroying half of Aeon's palace, and physically killing four changelings - at least one of those wasn't accidental and quite brutal. That's how we play Paladin's Legacy! That game was changed a lot about what I expect from good roleplaying game overall and really awesome game mastering in particular.<br /> <br /> There was also another game, but this is another story...<br /> <br /> Thanks for reading!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 03-17-2015, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T10:47:46-07:00","id":442818,"title":"","content":"Among other things is this webcomic I found not while ago, I wanted to share with those, who haven't seen it yet: <a href=\"http://chrysalis.thecomicseries.com/comics/first\" target=\"_blank\">http://chrysalis.thecomicseries.com/comics/first</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 03-17-2015, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T22:20:45-07:00","id":448837,"title":"","content":"I still play Changeling the Dreaming with my friends. It's a great game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T05:30:15-07:00","id":449020,"title":"","content":"There is anything in particular, you could share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T07:20:50-07:00","id":449239,"title":"","content":"It is hard to know where to begin. Our work-in-progress timeline (from May 2002 to October 2014, so far) is over 50 pages long in 10 font. We have played many different Changeling games, but all in the same world. Interestingly, in every game we have played (except the current one I'm running) an evil redcap super genius named Black Beret has appeared. He has been captured, frozen for years, but he always finds a way to escape and renew his unending campaign of evil. One of the characters in our games - a troll named Ulf - has become High King, but way back in 2002 he took an oath never to harm Black Beret. This oath - made in an early game - has vexed High King Ulf for over a decade. If any my players are reading this, rest assured Black Beret shall return!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T09:56:18-07:00","id":449411,"title":"","content":"Back in the long-ago, 1st Ed. Changeling came out. One of my long term players desperately wanted to play it as a respite from my grim Vampire games and grim-ish, intense Mage games. I obliged her.<br /> <br /> We set the game in the local area, using local landmarks, businesses and the occasional person (my MA advisor was cast as a satyr... he had a certain fondness for his female graduate students that had resulted in a series of marriages). The game began in media res, with all the players having apparently gone through Chrysalis at the same time in the same place. Unfortunately for them, that place was a museum, there was a prominent display case that had obviously been broken into and the alarm was going off... <br /> <br /> We managed to play a game with a lot of flashback scenes. As the characters discovered the extent of their amnesia, we ran scenes from their mortal lives that led up to that moment in the museum where someone opened a box and they all became changelings.<br /> <br /> I definitely ran the game more from being inspired by the Grimm's version of the Grimm's Fairy Tales, so.... not so &quot;fun&quot; really. The requestor played a sidhe and she ended up pledging herself to the Baroness of the local court. They discovered that she was &quot;under the spell&quot; of a vampire (they just knew him as &quot;the Dark Man&quot;) and that the way to disenchant her was to put someone's Glamour into the magic box that had gone missing from the museum back in Act I, Scene 1. The teenage crow pooka voluntarily made himself &quot;undone&quot;, contributing ALL his Glamour into the box (and forgetting everything about the others and the changeling world). The sidhe then had to trick the Baroness into opening the box. She was successful. The Baroness opened the box and was disenchanted, but tricking her liege definitely violated her oath of fealty. So she went blind. <br /> <br /> After the game was over, she said &quot;That wasn't fun.&quot; I asked if she meant &quot;funny&quot; as in light-hearted and amusing. She said, &quot;Yes.&quot; I asked if she thought it was a good story and if SHE had fun. She admitted that she did. And from that point forward it was well established that I just don't seem to be able to do &quot;funny&quot; for the sake of funny.<br /> <br /> But it was a good game. It ended up a part of the backstory of other, later games we played. (We're currently playing a Vampire game, based on a Mage game, which has that Changeling game as one of it's backdrops.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T05:27:08-07:00","id":450338,"title":"","content":"Both good stories to share. Thank you, Ajax, Cire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 03-20-2015, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T03:21:15-07:00","id":460881,"title":"","content":"And lo, a wild mistypaw appears. This seems a good a thread as any to say &quot;Hi, I just found this and made an account!&quot; ::waves:: It's been a long strange trip since I last played, which has been longer than I'd like. But it is what it is.<br /> Stories... well, you can thank me for the blurb in Kithbook: Pooka about pig latin. Back in the day people gave me trouble with whether that was a valid expression of the frailty or not. So I emailed to Jackie and Nicky and was amazed to actually be answered by the fine ladies.<br /> <br /> My first character, and probably best known one was Mistypaw, whose name I still use online. She was a pig latin speaking cat pooka who had a quirk that when she chrysalised and remembered her fae self, she forgot her mundane self. So she was a bit flighty and wandered around in and out of various stories and lovers. As I was young and a new gamer, she was comparatively a pretty simple character. But in my headcannon, she eventually stayed with her troll girlfriend Einmyria, whose plight and devotion inspired and impressed her. Misty made Ein feel lighthearted, happy, and free... except she had already sworn betrothal to another troll and he would not release her. The fallout hurt her quite a bit and it was odd, but Misty had to be the one to take care of someone else for once. Someone who paid a dear price to be true to her feelings for her. Though she had fleed previous engagements herself, Ein needed her and made her feel like more than just a stray.<br /> <br /> My other main character was Melitha, a sluagh childling who had been in lives past a rather dark character and she wonders if it was nature or circumstance. If this life might turn out better. Remembering so much of the past, she's rather mature in her head and has instincts and desires that are not age appropriate. Running from those who knew her in the past to give herself a chance to see if things could change, she travelled the childling underground railroad and wound up in St. Augustine, FL. That town might well be the home in her heart, but she had to go to a boarding school for childlings... for protection, they said. She used her skills to play the role of a vengance spirit in the school to manipulate and gather information from the students, and used that to get professors to teach her rarer arts not on the curriculum. And she dated a Fir-bholg that integrated himself into the school. Things were interesting, but the game went on hiatus and never finished.<br /> <br /> I wonder if someone started a game today, if I would ever find her an ending... or who I might make up next?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5509-mistypaw","name":"Mistypaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T10:59:10-07:00","id":461234,"title":"","content":"It was nice to hear about Mistypaw and Melitha. My they find a home (game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T11:33:39-07:00","id":461266,"title":"","content":"Mistypaw! It's good to see you posting again! (says the forumite formerly known as Julius_Patel).<br /> <br /> Let's see, my Changeling: The Dreaming origin story. At about the time that Vampire: The Masquerade revised came out, a friend of a friend invited me to play in their World of Darkness game. I had an absolute blast! So much so, I got a copy of Vampire and started up a World of Darkness game for some close friends. Everyone started as mortals with the possibility of becoming some sort of supernatural through play. All the players listed their top three supernaturals they wanted their character to become. One of the players listed her top choice as Changeling. At the time, I had never heard of the game, but she was super curious about. I picked up the core book to see what it was about. I couldn't put it down. The themes, the writing, the world, the kiths; I was in love! I created a pooka NPC to be her character's faerie mentor - Julia Patel. I loved playing the NPC, and she was a huge hit with the players. Later, when the player offered to run a solely Changeling game, I really wanted reprise the NPC, but I didn't feel comfortable playing an opposite gender PC at the time. One of the other players suggested playing her identical twin brother, Julius. So I did.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BymGBI7sN3MsNGViMmUyM2YtMzVlZC00MmE4LWFmMjItNzgyYjIwNjBhODRm/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Patel Twins</a> were born.<br /> <br /> Rough and as new as we all were, those still rank as some of my all time favorite chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 03-29-2015, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T16:39:27-07:00","id":461636,"title":"","content":"The Patel Twins seem great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:26:46-07:00","id":462875,"title":"","content":"You know, I am still waiting to play Changeling proper, but this topic title constantly makes me cringe and think of the wicked green stuff in Werewolf. What is Balefire in Changeling?<br /> <br /> (Oh and keep the stories going)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:44:19-07:00","id":462889,"title":"","content":"It's the yummy fire full of Glamour that burns at the heart of a Freehold and keeps bad bad Banality at bay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:07:08-07:00","id":463599,"title":"","content":"The only Changeling I've had the privilege to play was a moth-winged Sluaugh childling runaway. A well-meaning (but ultimately enabling) social worker kept him supplied with the anti-depressant drug that she was convinced was essential to his mental well-being (and to which he was addicted), even as he refused to stay in any foster home in which he was placed. When he underwent Chrysalis, his Irish-red hair started coming in dark at the roots; about an inch or two was visible in his mortal Seeming. His Faerie Mein had only the very tips of his hair still anything but black, but those tips almost burned with a coppery radiance in any ambient light.<br /> <br /> As with all his kith, he was quiet and curious. He tended to find his way into all sorts of places he may not have been wanted, and when a local Sidhe lord asked for volunteers for a quest which could range all over the land, he signed up. It's not like he had anything tying him down, and maybe travelling with older Fae would let him get away from all the authority figures that seemed to think kids should be in the banality-laden child services system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:44:29-07:00","id":464084,"title":"","content":"<b>Mistypaw, PookaKnight, Segev</b>, welcome to the thread. Nice characters, you have. Actually, I couldn't grasped that somewhat lighter (and sometimes, more dangerous) and childish side of Changelings. Like, all my characters, were adult and, usually, dangerous and secure (also <b>&quot;<a href=\"http://Darker and Edgier\" target=\"_blank\">darker and edgier</a>&quot;</b>), even while being seen as klutz/loosers by mortal standards.<br /> <br /> P.S. Patel twins are crazy awesome.<br /> <br /> Anyone here, had an experience, playing enchanted or kinain, BTW?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 03-31-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T07:22:52-07:00","id":464653,"title":"","content":"I ran a game one of the players played an enchanted police officer in Eugene, Oregon. It was a fun games, forcing me to play more attention to mortal things. I would also say that Segev's sluagh is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  forgot stuff 04-01-2015, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T13:22:47-07:00","id":471603,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I liked him in concept; sadly, the game didn't last very long.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the big danger for the little Sluagh was that he would drift away from the mortal world. The Fae world is more likely to accept a parentless childling than is the mortal society, and this would make it easier for him to run away to there. Bedlam, rather than banality, would likely be his greater threat.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, if he's caught up in the mortal world's jaws, the teeth would grind, gear-like, to impress banality on him. The necessary balance would be particularly hard to maintain. (And his drug addiction probably didn't help. I think it was Xanax, but it's been a while and I am not an expert on the oft overprescribed drugs that are &quot;safe&quot; to give kids diagnosed with mood disorders.)<br /> <br /> But being a Sluagh, he could get just about anywhere and obsessively collected bits and pieces of gossip and trivia and secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T16:31:57-07:00","id":545972,"title":"","content":"I'm currently playing in one CtD game and running another (hello, Mistypaw!). I'm enjoying it immensely. I've always loved the setting and had only ever played a few games back in the day. Playing again now has made me so happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T01:44:55-07:00","id":546668,"title":"","content":"My first experience was actually in a mage the ascension game where the storyteller allowed me to create and portray a changeling NPC. Sir Kelly the Morning Bright ap Fionna, Sidhe Wilder in the service of Queen Mary Elizabeth of the Kingdom of Grass. He pulled the Midsummer Night's Dream caper on the cabal, defeated a frost witch, routed out two Nephandi and teleported a couple of Black Spiral Dancers into low orbit, only for them to fall on his parent's house...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />....oops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:09:18-07:00","id":547916,"title":"","content":"Sadly I've never gotten to play in or run a solo CtD game.<br /> <br /> My first WoD game was a Werewolf game where I played a Fianna Ragabash, Tuatha De Fionn so in that game we had some crossover with Changelings, though (I know now) they were more inspired by CtD instead of following it closely.<br /> Since then I've run more than a couple of crossovers over the years with 1 of my players favoring playing Changelings (a polar bear Pooka and 2 different Sidhe). They've worked well enough as long as rules for how things interact are decided beforehand. The characters were really interesting, and fun to see played. Though I attribute that as much on the player as on the system.<br /> <br /> A couple of months ago I planned out short introductory stories (1-2 sessions each) for my gaming group for a few of the WoD games (Hunter, Vampire, Changeling and Werewolf). We got through the first 2, but the week before the Changeling game, 2 out of the 4 players moved away so we never got to start . I still plan on running it at some point but for now it's been put on hold.<br /> I really like the Changeling setting and themes, and I've collected most of the game line's books so I'm looking forward to actually getting to use them at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}